desc: Zero Tolerance Thru-Zero Flanger (mda ThruZero port) by chmaha
tags: flanger thru-zero chorus modulation
author: chmaha
version: 1.0
changelog:
  Initial release.
about:
  Classic tape-style thru-zero flanger. A short delayed copy of the signal sweeps back and forth and is
  subtracted from the dry signal, so at the top of each sweep the two line up and cancel: the "thru-zero"
  point that tape flanging is known for. Rate sets the sweep time (all the way down switches the LFO off
  for a static comb), Depth sets how far it sweeps, and Depth Mod sets how much of that sweep moves: at
  100% it sweeps right down to zero delay, lower values keep a minimum delay to stop low-frequency
  build-up with high feedback. Feedback can be positive or negative. Four presets from the original are
  one click away: Thru-Zero Flanger, Phase Canceller, Chorus Doubler and Mad Modulator.
  Ported from mda ThruZero by Paul Kellett (Maxim Digital Audio), via mda-effects
  https://github.com/pluginguru/mda-effects (MIT or GPLv2+)
  JSFX version released under GPLv3+ license
  Claude generated some of this code
